<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to May 14 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.34)	 one year     0.38 (0.37)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.34 (0.34)	 two years    0.56 (0.50)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.35)	 three years  1.01 (0.94)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.33 (0.32)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.51 (0.45)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.30 (0.30)	 three years  0.95 (0.89)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.29 (0.27)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.46 (0.40)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.25 (0.25)	 three years  0.90 (0.84)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, May 12 - May 16:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.54 (0.55)   120-150 days  0.51 (0.58)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.55 (0.55)   150-180 days  UNQ  (0.52)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.56 (0.56)   180-360 days  0.63 (0.54)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.58 (0.57)   over 360 days 0.84 (0.75)</p>
